  message: "OWNER RULING 2026-08-03: KEEP ORM reads as sources, but make them SEPARABLE in the output. Do not drop them.\n\nShape: ORM reads carry a distinct taint label (data at rest in the database) from genuinely external input (wire, env, argv, socket). Same flows found; the two become distinguishable so a reader can filter, rather than the tool deciding silently for them. Sequencing: this is QUEUED BEHIND WI-bifob (owner ruling, same interview); re-rank it against WI-kabif section 3a on fresh numbers after WI-bifob lands, not on the argument below.\n\nCORRECTIONS TO THIS ITEM'S OWN FILING, measured on the same cohort-joruv arm the filing used.\n\n1. THE FILING'S CENTRAL ARGUMENT IS REFUTED. It states: \"This class is 28.2 percent of rows on its own and is the reason several claims are saturated at violated. Precision work cannot make a saturated disjunction informative; scoping decisions can.\" Measured: dropping the ENTIRE ORM class changes ZERO of 18 violated claim verdicts. Every claim it touches retains other, non-ORM evidence holding it violated. So this class is NOT why any claim is saturated, and the ranking argument that put this item ahead of section 3a does not hold for this item. Section 3a's pre-registered effect is also zero verdict changes -- on that axis the two are tied, and the honest remaining case for this item is output READABILITY, not verdict correctness.\n\n2. SCOPE-AXIS ERROR IN THE TITLE AND FILING (L1, the WI-duguk shape). \"28.2 percent of cohort findings\" reads as a cohort-wide property. It is ONE REPO: all 89 strict ORM-read-to-ORM-write rows are pretix, the only Django application in the cohort. Zero in caddy, alertmanager, kserve, express, apollo-server. Every number in the filing is real and generalized along the wrong dimension; the axis is (framework, repo), not (cohort).\n\n3. TWO PREDICATES, TWO NUMBERS, BOTH CORRECT. The filed 28.2 percent (100 of 354) counts rows with an ORM-WRITE SINK regardless of source. The strict read-to-write pairing -- an ORM read source AND an ORM write sink, which is what the title actually describes -- is 89 of 354, 25.1 percent. Reproduced both. State which predicate whenever quoting the number.\n\n4. INDEPENDENT OF WI-bifob, which had been described alongside it as \"roughly half the output\" jointly. Overlap is 10 rows (2.8 percent). Union is exactly 177 of 354 (50.0 percent). Two separate decisions.\n\n5. CAP CAVEAT. pretix/untrusted-input-no-database holds exactly 100 evidence rows, an output cap. Per-claim conclusions on that claim are unreliable, and any filtering changes WHICH 100 rows are shown rather than how many."  # 0cfd
